t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Today, President Donald J. Trump returns to the Buckeye State to showcase a record of results that puts Ohio workers, families, seniors, farmers, and communities first.</strong> Under the leadership of President Trump and Republicans, Ohioans are benefiting from historic tax relief, falling crime, surging private investment, stronger rural healthcare, and new resources for the state’s defense industry.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-delivering-historic-tax-relief-for-ohioans\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Delivering Historic Tax Relief for Ohioans</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s Working Families Tax Cuts are putting real money back in the pockets of hardworking Ohio workers, families, and seniors.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Overtime:</strong> More than 1.2 million Ohio workers <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-ceo-frank-j-bisignano-visits-ohio-to-tout-working-families-tax-cuts-provisions-on-no-tax-on-car-loan-interest-no-tax-on-overtime-enhanced-deduction-for-senior-citizens#:~:text=More%20than%201.2%20million%20Ohio%20filers%20claimed%20the%20overtime%20deduction%2C%20totaling%20about%20%243.4%20billion.%20Nationally%2C%20about%2029.4%20million%20filers%20claimed%20the%20deduction%20totaling%20almost%20%2492.7%20billion.\">claimed</a> $3.4 billion in No Tax on Overtime deductions in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong> More than 1.5 million Ohio seniors <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-ceo-frank-j-bisignano-visits-ohio-to-tout-working-families-tax-cuts-provisions-on-no-tax-on-car-loan-interest-no-tax-on-overtime-enhanced-deduction-for-senior-citizens#:~:text=About%201.4%20million%20Ohioans%20benefitted%20from%20the%20senior%20deduction%2C%20with%20the%20total%20amount%20of%20deductions%20claimed%20approaching%20%247.9%20billion.%20Nationally%2C%20over%2035%20million%20seniors%20benefitted%20from%20the%20deduction%20with%20more%20than%20%24193%20billion%20claimed.\">benefited</a> from the new senior deduction in 2026, with the average senior expected to pay zero federal taxes on Social Security benefits.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong> Ohio taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$3,308</a> in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs and Wages:</strong> The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=37\">safeguarded</a> 208,000 Ohio jobs, $37 billion in state GDP, and $19 billion in wages for Ohioans.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Lowering Taxes for Small Businesses and Family Farms:</strong> The tax cuts permanently <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/INVESTS-IN-RURAL-AMERICA.pdf\">locked in</a> the increased death tax exemption (indexed for inflation), 100% expensing, a doubled Section 179 limit, and the 20% small business deduction. They also expanded crop insurance and raised reference prices for the first time in over a decade.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-strengthening-rural-healthcare-across-ohio\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Strengthening Rural Healthcare Across Ohio</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is delivering targeted resources to expand access, modernize care, and improve outcomes in Ohio’s rural communities.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Rural Health Transformation:</strong> Ohio <a href=\"https://governor.ohio.gov/media/news-and-media/governor-dewine-announces-ohios-rural-health-transformation-program-award\">secured</a> more than $200 million in first-year funding under the Working Families Tax Cuts’ Rural Health Transformation Program.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Modernizing Care:</strong> The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/trump-administration-announces-92-million-coordinate-rural-hospital-networks-improve-maternal-care\">awarded</a> $92 million across 22 rural Ohio hospitals to support coordinated care networks, maternal health services, and equipment and facilities upgrades.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-making-ohio-communities-safer\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making Ohio Communities Safer</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Violent crime is falling across Ohio as President Trump’s law and order agenda takes hold.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Statewide homicides <a href=\"https://www.daytondailynews.com/local/crime/new-fbi-data-crime-rate-drops-across-us-ohio/article_bf55b67f-c59b-57a8-87da-831ababfb790.html\">dropped</a> 16.1% last year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Columbus</strong> <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/local/columbus/2026/01/08/2025-homicides-crime-trends-ohio\">hit</a> a 16-year low in homicides in 2025, with <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\">further declines</a> in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cincinnati</strong> saw homicides <a href=\"https://spectrumnews1.com/oh/columbus/news/2026/02/03/cincinnati-sees-drop-in-crimes-in-2025\">fall</a> more than 6% in 2025 and <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\">drop</a> another 19% in the first half of 2026 compared with the same period the year before.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cleveland</strong> recorded double-digit <a href=\"https://www.police1.com/police-recruitment/cleveland-crime-drops-as-police-see-356-rise-in-cadet-applications\">drops</a> in 2025: homicides down 16%, rapes down 28%, auto thefts down 26%, and robberies down 24%. In the first half of 2026, rapes fell another 8% and robberies another 21%.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-unleashing-private-investment-and-job-creation\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Unleashing Private Investment and Job Creation</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s pro-growth, America First policies are drawing major private investment and new jobs across the Buckeye State.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Nvidia</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/17/nvidia-financing-open-ai-data-center-ohio.html\">financing</a> up to $105 billion for a new Super Intelligence data center in Pike County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Electra</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.jobsohio.com/newsroom/news-press/electra-to-usher-in-the-next-era-of-aviation-with-advanced-production-facility-in-springfield-ohio\">investing</a> $850 million to open its first EL9 Ultra Short aircraft production facility in Springfield, creating 1,975 new jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Stellantis</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.13abc.com/2025/10/15/new-midsize-truck-be-assembled-toledo-part-nearly-400-million-stellantis-investment/\">investing</a> $400 million in its Toledo Assembly Complex, creating over 900 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bayer</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.jobsohio.com/newsroom/news-press/bayer-to-invest-22-billion-in-a-new-manufacturing-site-in-ohio\">investing</a> $2.2 billion to build a pharmaceutical manufacturing campus in New Albany, creating about 600 permanent jobs and 1,500 construction jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honda</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/honda-plans-invest-25-bln-build-hybrid-vehicle-plant-ohio-nikkei-says-2026-09-24/\">investing</a> up to $2.5 billion to build a new hybrid vehicle production plant in Ohio. </li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Hikma Pharmaceuticals</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.jobsohio.com/newsroom/news-press/hikma-pharmaceuticals-announces-major-expansion-in-ohio-creating-350-new-jobs-and-investing-267-million\">investing</a> $267 million to expand its manufacturing facilities in Columbus and Bedford, creating 350 new jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Weidmann</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.journal-news.com/local/manufacturer-plans-150m-investment-at-former-middletown-paper-mill-creating-56-jobs/article_0d0c3615-cd66-58b6-8485-e725f2651142.html\">investing</a> $150 million to renovate and expand a historic former paper mill in Middletown, creating dozens of new full-time jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Kreate</strong> is <a href=\"https://www.plasticstoday.com/injection-molding/kreate-announces-100-million-ohio-manufacturing-facility-investment\">investing</a> $100 million for a new consumer and professional plastic products manufacturing facility in Tiffin.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Kimberly-Clark</strong> is <a href=\"https://businessjournaldaily.com/a-factory-for-the-future/\">investing</a> $800 million to build its first new U.S. plant in 37 years in Warren.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Vallourec</strong> is <a href=\"https://businessjournaldaily.com/vallourec-invests-48m-in-youngstown-expansion/\">investing</a> $48 million to expand its operations in Youngstown.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-powering-growth-and-protecting-communities\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Powering Growth and Protecting Communities</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is securing reliable energy and delivering for communities that were neglected under the previous Administration.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Protecting Ratepayers:</strong> The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.energy.gov/articles/fact-sheet-department-energy-ensuring-affordable-energy-access-ohio-while-powering-future/\">formed</a> a public-private partnership with SoftBank Group and SB Energy to build 10 gigawatts of new power generation in southern Ohio, ensuring corporations — not Ohio families — pay the costs of data center growth. The deal includes $40 million in community benefits from SB Energy.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Standing Up for East Palestine:</strong> After years of inaction, the Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.hhs.gov/press-room/nih-long-term-health-research-east-palestine-ohio-train-disaster.html\">launched</a> a five-year, $10 million research initiative to study the long-term health impacts of the 2023 train derailment and ensure residents receive the medical attention they need.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Revitalizing American Steelmaking:</strong> The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.energy.gov/articles/energy-department-announces-500-million-award-revitalize-american-steelmaking\">awarded</a> $500 million to <a href=\"https://www.cincinnati.com/story/news/politics/2026/08/21/jd-vance-announces-grant-middletown-steel-plant/91308063007/?gnt-cfr=1&amp;gca-cat=p&amp;gca-uir=false&amp;gca-epti=z1157xxp003950l001050c003950u003942e1157xxv001942&amp;gca-ft=180&amp;gca-ds=sophi\">support</a> a $1 billion investment at Cleveland-Cliffs’ Middletown Works facility in Middletown, protecting 2,300 jobs and strengthening our domestic steel supply chain.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-strengthening-ohio-s-defense-industry\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Strengthening Ohio’s Defense Industry</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is expanding Ohio’s role in national security and high-tech defense manufacturing.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>In October, President Trump <a href=\"https://thehill.com/newsletters/defense-national-security/6146728-cleveland-to-be-home-of-next-submarine-repair-center/\">announced</a> that Cleveland will be <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2109801412066443765?a=cmtp3_OzD8JOlMq4-eY&amp;s=20\">home</a> to the new U.S. Submarine Component Repair Center.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The first Ohio-built Fury fighter drone for the U.S. Air Force <a href=\"https://www.jobsohio.com/newsroom/news-press/first-ohio-built-fury-rolls-off-andurils-arsenal-1-production-line\">rolled off</a> the line in July at Anduril’s Arsenal-1 plant in Pickaway County — a $910.5 million project expected to create more than 4,000 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The FY 2026 NDAA <a href=\"https://www.moreno.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/moreno-delivers-over-72m-in-defense-wins-for-ohio/\">provided</a> more than $72 million for Ohio defense projects, including $60 million for work at Wright-Patterson Air Force Base.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump and Republicans are delivering for Ohio families, workers, seniors, and communities — proving once again that America First means Ohio First.</strong> Ohioans face a clear choice: continue this progress or return to the higher taxes, open borders, and failed policies of the past.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/president-trump-returns-to-ohio-with-a-record-of-results/\">President Trump Returns to Ohio With a Record of Results</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
